  "summary": "PAYLOAD ransomware operators hijacked Active Directory Group Policy, authoring a domain-root GPO named PAYLOAD that dropped ransom notes, replaced wallpaper/lock screen, enforced a logon banner and disabled local administrator accounts domain-wide without any malicious binary on endpoints. A second GPO ('win Firewall Off') disabled Windows Firewall, and data was exfiltrated before a one-day delayed detonation on reboot. Detection depends on directory service change auditing (5136/5137/5141) and SYSVOL integrity monitoring rather than file/process indicators.",
